/-- **`cor:lef`** (tex l.453–461): a finitely generated group is LEF if and only if it is a
subgroup of an infinite, finitely generated, simple Kazhdan group that is an expander limit of the
finite simple groups `SL_N(F₂)`; every finitely generated LEF group `Γ` lies in such a group whose
word problem has the Turing degree of that of `Γ`; so `Γ` has solvable word problem if and only if it
is a subgroup of such a group with solvable word problem.  Conjuncts: the five `SK12.corLef_*`
endpoints. -/
theorem cor_lef :
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corLef_lefIffSubgroupOfHost ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corLef_hostWithSameTuringDegree ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corLef_lefIffSubgroupOfSameTuringDegreeHost ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corLef_solvableWordProblemIffSubgroupOfHost ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corLef_lefSolvableWordProblemIffSubgroupOfHost :=
  ⟨@Full.SK12.corLef_lefIffSubgroupOfHost, @Full.SK12.corLef_hostWithSameTuringDegree,
    @Full.SK12.corLef_lefIffSubgroupOfSameTuringDegreeHost,
    @Full.SK12.corLef_solvableWordProblemIffSubgroupOfHost,
    @Full.SK12.corLef_lefSolvableWordProblemIffSubgroupOfHost⟩

/-- **`cor:host`** (tex l.463–470): every countable LEF group is a subgroup of such a group; the
members of a set of finitely generated groups embed in a single such group if and only if they are
LEF and represent countably many isomorphism classes; so one such group contains every recursively
presented finitely generated LEF group, for instance every finitely presented residually finite group
and every `G_Y` with `L(Y)` recursive.  Conjuncts: `SK12.corHost_countableLEFSubgroupOfHost`,
`SK12.corHost_familyEmbedsIffLEFCountableClasses`, `SK12.corHost_recursivelyPresentedInstances`. -/
theorem cor_host :
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corHost_countableLEFSubgroupOfHost ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corHost_familyEmbedsIffLEFCountableClasses.{u} ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK12.corHost_recursivelyPresentedInstances :=
  ⟨@Full.SK12.corHost_countableLEFSubgroupOfHost,
    @Full.SK12.corHost_familyEmbedsIffLEFCountableClasses.{u},
    @Full.SK12.corHost_recursivelyPresentedInstances⟩

/-- **`lem:nn`** (tex l.489–492): every countable LEF group is a subgroup of `[Δ, Δ]` for an
infinite LEF group `Δ` generated by two elements.  Conjuncts: `SK09.lemmaNN` and the steps of its
proof (tex l.494–525): the commutator computation, the power differences, the level-zero word, and
