/-- **`cor:wp`** (tex l.683–690): the word problem of `G_X` has the Turing degree of the language
`L(X)`, so `G_X` has solvable word problem if and only if `L(X)` is recursive, as for the Fibonacci
subshift; every Turing degree is the degree of the word problem of some `G_X`; and there is a family
of continuum many groups `G_X`, none of which embeds in another.

Conjuncts: the closed `SK13.corollary` and `SK13.corollary_explicit`; `SK13.wp_degree_eq_language`;
`SK13.wp_solvable_iff_recursive`; `SK13.fibonacci_wp_solvable`; `SK13.every_degree`; and
`SK13.continuum_antichain`. -/
theorem cor_wp :
    type_of% @Full.SK13.corollary ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.corollary_explicit ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.wp_degree_eq_language ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.wp_solvable_iff_recursive ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.fibonacci_wp_solvable ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.every_degree ∧
    type_of% @Full.SK13.continuum_antichain :=
